 "etapas": [
  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Comparing with something unreal",
     "texto": [
      "**Como si** compares with something that is not true. The verb that follows goes in the **past subjunctive**:\n\n- Habla **como si fuera** el jefe. (he is not)\n- Me mira **como si estuviera** loco. (he is not)\n\nIf the comparison looks at something earlier, use **hubiera** + participle:\n\n- Estás pálido, **como si hubieras visto** un fantasma.\n\nThe main verb can be in any tense: habla, hablaba, habló **como si fuera** el dueño."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "«Como si», «ni que» and their neighbours",
     "texto": [
      "**Como si** + **imperfect subjunctive** compares with something unreal happening at the same time: habla como si lo **supiera**.\n\n**Como si** + **hubiera** + participle compares with something unreal that came before: como si **hubiera visto** un fantasma.\n\nIt never takes the present subjunctive or the indicative.\n\nIn colloquial language: **¡Ni que** + imperfect subjunctive**!** ¡Ni que fuera gratis!\n\nTwo similar expressions take the **indicative**:\n\n- **Parece que** va a llover.\n- **Hace como que** no me ve. Finge que no me ve."
     ],
